      "body": "Verified the key facts myself: single **Tesla T4 (15 GB)**, currently **12.4 GB still held by a stale kernel process (PID 662721)**; PEFT 0.18.1, torch 2.9.1, Lightning 2.6.6.\n\nThe diagnosis is solid. The failing 1.25 GiB allocation is exactly `(1, 65536, 5120)` in **fp32** \u2014 the `mlp.fc2` input, upcast from bf16 back to fp32 by PEFT's `_cast_input_dtype` (`peft/tuners/lora/layer.py:805`) because your LoRA weights are fp32. It dies during *gradient-checkpoint recomputation in backward*, so `checkpoint_layers: [0..9]` is already maxed out, and `batch_size: 1` / `lora r: 2` are already at floor. A few questions before I finalize the approach.",
