              "questions": "[{\"question\":\"A 15 GB T4 with the 2D head (65,536 tokens \u2192 4096\u00d74096 decoder) is genuinely tight. Which precision strategy do you want?\",\"header\":\"Precision route\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"bf16-true (max headroom)\",\"description\":\"Trainer precision=\\\"bf16-true\\\": casts all weights to bf16. Saves ~0.7 GB params + ~1.7 GB of checkpointed block inputs, and makes the PEFT upcast a no-op. Est. peak ~6-7 GB. Caveat: the 169M-param spectral complex_weight gets bf16-rounded (~0.4% relative), slightly degrading pretrained fidelity.\"},{\"label\":\"bf16-mixed + kill PEFT upcast\",\"description\":\"Keep fp32 master weights, but set cast_input_dtype_enabled=False on LoRA layers so activations stay bf16. Numerically safest, but only saves ~0.6-1.3 GB at peak \u2014 est. ~9 GB, may still OOM on a bad fragmentation day.\"},{\"label\":\"Staged: try safe first, fall back\",\"description\":\"Implement both switches, run the safe one (bf16-mixed + no upcast) with a memory probe, and flip to bf16-true only if it still OOMs. More work, but you get measured numbers instead of estimates.\"}]},{\"question\":\"Is any GPU larger than this T4 available to you? It changes how aggressively we need to compromise.\",\"header\":\"Hardware\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"T4 only \u2014 must fit 15 GB\",\"description\":\"Plan around the single 15 GB T4. Every lever on the table, including reducing effective resolution if needed.\"},{\"label\":\"Larger GPU available\",\"description\":\"I can get an A100/H100 or similar. Plan the memory fixes as good hygiene, but don't compromise model fidelity to squeeze into 15 GB.\"},{\"label\":\"Not sure / check for me\",\"description\":\"Investigate what's reachable from this environment before committing.\"}]},{\"question\":\"Should the fixes go only in the notebook, or also into the shared infrastructure?\",\"header\":\"Scope\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Notebook + shared infra\",\"description\":\"Fix the sf_triggers notebook AND plumb the knobs properly: a training.precision config field, PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF in the entry points, prefetch_factor in builders.py, plus a memory-troubleshooting section in the docs. Matches CLAUDE.md's reusability directive and fixes 3_finetune_template_1D.py too.\"},{\"label\":\"Notebook only (fastest)\",\"description\":\"Get sf_triggers/2_finetune_template_1D.ipynb running now; leave workshop_infrastructure/ untouched.\"},{\"label\":\"Notebook + script, no config plumbing\",\"description\":\"Fix both sf_triggers entry points with hardcoded values; skip new config fields and docs.\"}]}]"
            },
