      "body": "The plan is written. Summary of what the investigation found \u2014 my initial read was partly wrong, and the corrections matter:\n\n**Root cause (confirmed by direct reproduction):** the 1.25 GiB allocation is `mlp.fc2`'s input tensor `(1, 65536, 5120)` in **fp32**. PEFT upcasts the bf16 activation back to fp32 to match `lora_A.weight.dtype`, then autocast immediately casts it back down \u2014 the copy buys nothing, and it's charged on every gradient-checkpoint recompute of every block.\n\n**Three corrections to my first read:**\n\n1. **bf16 is the wrong dtype for this GPU.** `is_bf16_supported(including_emulation=False)` is `False` on SM75 \u2014 the T4 emulates bf16. At this model's MLP GEMM shape: fp16 9.3 ms, fp32 56.8 ms, **bf16 90.1 ms**. The current `bf16-mixed` pays a 60% slowdown vs plain fp32 for its memory saving. `16-mixed` is identical on memory and ~6\u00d7 faster.\n2. **`bf16-true` would silently break Adam** \u2014 Lightning casts the module before building the optimizer, so `exp_avg_sq` lives in bf16 where the `beta2=0.999` update falls below mantissa resolution. Measured: a parameter of magnitude 1.0 doesn't move at all over 20 steps. It's off the table.\n3. **`pos_embed` is a fp32 *buffer*** (`embedding.py:113`), added to a half-precision tensor at `:124`, which pins the residual stream to fp32 across all 10 blocks \u2014 3.44 GiB instead of 1.72 GiB in the 11 live token tensors. Casting frozen params *and buffers* to fp16 is worth ~2.5 GiB.\n\nAlso: `lora_dropout: 0.1` is costing 1.4\u20132.2 GiB (PEFT builds `nn.Identity` at `p=0.0`, `nn.Dropout` otherwise \u2014 and on `fc2` that output is the 65536\u00d75120 tensor again). One YAML character.\n\nTwo things worth knowing before you approve: **12.2 GiB is still held by the dead kernel right now** (only 2.55 GiB free), so a restart is a hard prerequisite. And resolution reduction / `complex_weight` interpolation is *not* needed \u2014 Phase 1+2 land at ~8.5\u20139 GiB with ~6 GiB headroom.\n\n`AskUserQuestion` is disabled in this session, so I made two calls you may want to override: I planned for T4-only, and I included the shared-infra plumbing (config `precision` field, `builders.py` `prefetch_factor`, docs) per CLAUDE.md's reusability directive. Phase 1+2 alone unblock the notebook if you'd rather keep the diff small.",
