      "body": "CUDA tolerates it; CPU raises. The Plan agent's audit was CUDA-only. The right fix is to exclude normalization layers from the cast \u2014 that's standard mixed-precision practice anyway (norms stay fp32 for stability), costs almost nothing, and keeps the notebook's CPU smoke test working:",
      "id": "8c0273ae-e426-4aef-8b00-0d7e3dd69693",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
