      "id": "b8791d31-478d-4d41-8809-7466eaad0504",
      "mentions": []
    },
    {
      "body": "Here's where things stand while the second epoch finishes.\n\n## The OOM is fixed, verified at the real config on your T4\n\n| configuration | peak allocated | outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| your settings (`bf16-mixed`, PEFT cast on, `lora_dropout 0.1`) | 13.37 GiB | **OOM** \u2014 reproduced exactly |\n| after the fix | **10.05 GiB** | runs, 2.8 GiB headroom |\n\nThe real training run is live: epoch 0 completed all 8 batches with loss falling 0.103 \u2192 0.081, and trainable params are 706,816 \u2014 identical to before, so the fine-tuning regime is unchanged.\n\n**Root cause:** the 1.25 GiB allocation was `mlp.fc2`'s input `(1, 65536, 5120)` in **fp32**. PEFT upcast the bf16 activation to match its fp32 adapter weights, and autocast immediately cast it back down \u2014 a pure-waste copy, billed at the widest tensor in the network, on every gradient-checkpoint recompute.\n\n## Three places the plan was wrong, corrected by measurement\n\n- **bf16 is the wrong dtype for a T4.** `is_bf16_supported(including_emulation=False)` is `False` on SM75 \u2014 it's emulated. At this model's MLP GEMM shape: fp16 9.3 ms, fp32 56.8 ms, **bf16 90.1 ms**. Your `bf16-mixed` was paying a 60% slowdown *versus no mixed precision at all*. Now `16-mixed`.\n- **The biggest single lever wasn't in the plan.** `dual_ln_full` returns fp32 (LayerNorm always does under autocast), so `k`/`v` stayed fp32 through a 4\u00d7 overlapping-tile `.contiguous()` expansion. One `.to(q.dtype)` in `transformer_ls.py:105-106` is worth **\u22121.39 GiB** \u2014 more than everything else combined. Note the plan's suggested `.to(k.dtype)` would have been a no-op.\n- **Two predicted levers are worth nothing.** `lora_dropout: 0.0` saved 5 MiB, not 1.4\u20132.2 GiB; `ft_checkpoint_head` saved exactly 0. Under checkpointing those tensors never coexist with the peak. I corrected the numbers I'd written into the config comments and docs rather than leave the overstated ones in.\n\n`bf16-true` is deliberately excluded: Lightning casts the module before building the optimizer, so Adam's `exp_avg_sq` lands in bf16 and stops accumulating \u2014 a parameter of magnitude 1.0 measurably doesn't move at all while the loss curve still looks healthy.\n\n## Two pre-existing bugs found on the way\n\n`downstream_apps/sf_triggers/3_finetune_template_1D.py` **had never been runnable**. It imported the template's config loader, which rejects this app's four `data:` keys, and passed a `label_transform` its dataset doesn't accept. Both fixed \u2014 otherwise my mirrored edits there would have been untestable.\n\nAlso: torch 2.9 warns that `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` is deprecated in favour of `PYTORCH_ALLOC_CONF`. **Don't act on that warning** \u2014 I verified via `memory_snapshot()[\"is_expandable\"]` that the new name is silently ignored for this setting on 2.9.1. Documented in-line so nobody \"fixes\" it and quietly disables expandable segments (worth 1.25 GiB of headroom here).\n\n## What changed\n\nTwo helpers in `workshop_infrastructure/utils.py` (`disable_peft_input_dtype_cast`, `cast_frozen_to`), a `training.precision` / `accumulate_grad_batches` config field with validation, `prefetch_factor` in `builders.py`, the vendored `transformer_ls.py` fix, both entry-point scripts, the notebook (including a `probe_step_memory()` cell so levers get measured rather than guessed), and a GPU Memory section in CLAUDE.md. **65 tests pass**, up from 56 \u2014 the new ones pin the dtype contract, the norm-layer exclusion, and the 2D decoder path.\n\nOne deviation worth flagging: `cast_frozen_to` skips normalization layers. The plan's audit said half LayerNorm weights were fine, but that was CUDA-only \u2014 on CPU `F.layer_norm` raises `mixed dtype (CPU): expect parameter to have scalar type of Float`, which would have broken the notebook's pre-GPU smoke test. Norm params are `2 \u00d7 embed_dim` each, so holding them at fp32 costs nothing and is the standard rule anyway.\n\n`black`/`isort`/`mypy` aren't installed in `surya_ws`, so I couldn't run the lint commands from CLAUDE.md; I checked the 100-char limit manually and all over-length lines are pre-existing.Epoch 0 finished with `val_loss=0.095` \u2014 so the validation path works too \u2014 and epoch 1 is progressing with training loss falling (0.081 \u2192 0.057). My filter included `val_loss=`, which now matches nearly every progress line, so let me tighten it to terminal states only:",
